# Keep the build context small AND prevent dev/test/secret artefacts from
# being baked into the image. Anything excluded here is invisible to the
# `COPY` instructions in the Dockerfile.

# --- Python build/runtime detritus -----------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Local virtualenvs (must NEVER be copied — wrong arch & polluted) ------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Test code & fixtures (not part of the runtime image) ------------------
tests/
pptx/

# --- Build-time/CI tooling (not part of the runtime image) -----------------
# tools/ci/* is the CI gate + evidence pipeline, run by GitHub Actions and
# tests/, never by the service. It also imports defusedxml, which is a dev-only
# pin and therefore absent from the production venv. The Dockerfile does not
# COPY it either; this entry is the defence-in-depth half, matching tests/ and
# skills/ above. It used to live at agents/ci/ and so WAS baked into the image
# by `COPY agents/`.
tools/

# --- Per-user runtime data (bind-mounted from the host at runtime) ---------
# In production /app/skills is an EBS volume, NOT baked image content.
skills/

# --- Secrets & local configuration (NEVER bake into images) ----------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- Documentation (the runtime image doesn't serve docs) ------------------
*.md
README*
# ...EXCEPT agents/ AGENT.md + guardrail .md — these are runtime DATA the agent
# loader reads from disk (not docs). Re-include so `COPY agents/` keeps them.
!agents/**/*.md

# --- Git metadata ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Docker artefacts (avoid recursive context bloat) ----------------------
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml

# --- Editor / OS / misc paranoia ------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
node_modules/
